## 10. Critical Audit & SOTA Enhancements

The following is a rigorous, adversarial audit of the plan itself, identifying gaps, weaknesses, and novel improvements.

### 10.1 Gaps Identified & Mitigated

| # | Gap | Severity | Mitigation |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| 1 | **No network timeout on remote version check.** Guardian's `fetch()` to GitHub could hang indefinitely on poor connections. | 🟡 | Add `AbortController` with 10-second timeout to all remote fetches. |
| 2 | **`npm install` runs arbitrary `postinstall` scripts.** A compromised dependency could execute code during install, before our security gates run. | 🔴 | Run `npm install --ignore-scripts` first, then `npm rebuild` only for known-safe native modules (`sqlite3`, `node-pty`). Log which scripts would have run. |
| 3 | **Git pull over HTTPS could be MITM'd on untrusted networks.** | 🟡 | Document recommendation to use SSH remotes. Verify `git remote get-url origin` uses `git@github.com:` or `https://github.com/`. Warn if remote URL is unexpected. |
| 4 | **No rate limiting on update checks.** Guardian checks every 30 min, UI checks on load, CLI can check on demand — could hit GitHub rate limits. | 🟢 | Cache the last check result with a 15-minute TTL. Guardian result is shared with `/api/update/check`. |
| 5 | **Auto-update could trigger during active operator session.** Operator is mid-conversation when Guardian fires auto-update. | 🟡 | Auto-update will only trigger if the operator presence status is `"away"` or if there are zero active chat sessions. If sessions are active, defer and re-check in 30 minutes. |
| 6 | **No changelog visibility.** Operator clicks UPDATE but has no idea what's in the new version. | 🟢 | Future enhancement: Fetch the diff of `CHANGELOG.md` between `oldVersion` and `newVersion` and display it in the confirmation dialog. |
| 7 | **Backup directory could grow unbounded.** Each update creates a new backup. | 🟢 | Retain only the 5 most recent backups. Prune older ones during Phase 3. |
| 8 | **No checksum verification of the remote `package.json` response.** A CDN cache poisoning attack could return a fake version. | 🟡 | Cross-verify: fetch both `raw.githubusercontent.com` AND run `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/main` to compare the remote HEAD commit. If they disagree, warn. |
| 9 | **DB migration could fail halfway through multiple databases.** | 🟡 | Already mitigated: each migration runs in its own SQLite transaction. Failed migration auto-rollbacks. But we should also skip WAL-locked databases and retry. |
| 10 | **Windows file locking.** `*.db-wal` and `*.db-shm` files may be locked if the server didn't shut down cleanly. | 🟡 | Add a 3-second retry loop for file copy operations on Windows. Use `fs.copyFile` with error handling. |

### 10.2 SOTA Enhancements (Novel Contributions)

| # | Enhancement | Value |
|:---|:---|:---|
| 1 | **Guardian as Update Sentinel.** No other local AI framework has an autonomous agent that proactively monitors for updates and notifies the operator. This is a novel, world-class pattern. |
| 2 | **Security-gated update pipeline.** Running governance signature verification (`verify-governance-signature.cjs --strict`) and PAD integrity checks as update gates is unprecedented in the Node.js ecosystem. Most frameworks blindly pull and build. |
| 3 | **`npm install --ignore-scripts` + selective rebuild.** This is a SOTA supply-chain defense. By running `--ignore-scripts` first, we prevent arbitrary code execution from compromised dependencies. We then selectively rebuild only known-safe native modules. |
| 4 | **Cross-verified version check.** Using both `raw.githubusercontent.com` AND `git ls-remote` to verify version consistency provides defense-in-depth against CDN cache poisoning — a novel approach. |
| 5 | **Session-aware auto-update.** Deferring auto-update when operator sessions are active prevents mid-conversation disruption. This is a thoughtful UX pattern not seen in comparable platforms. |
| 6 | **Unified rollback event schema.** Both update rollbacks and runtime security rollbacks emit the same Activity Bus format, giving the Guardian a single lens through which to monitor all state reversals. |

### 10.3 Future Considerations (Not Blocking v1)

| Enhancement | Description |
|:---|:---|
| **Signed releases** | Verify GPG signatures on git tags before applying. |
| **Update channels** | Support `stable` / `beta` / `nightly` channels. |
